  "obligation": "Proper return_call, return_call_indirect and return_call_ref on the existing shared activation stack, including cross-program ownership and native root disposal.",
  "representation": "Terminal Wasm calls use the existing RETURN_REGISTER flag and call ABI. Lowering marks their path dead and forwards the callee result bundle directly. Same-program known/user calls recycle the active frame. Foreign user calls select the original callable program/environment/realm before replacement; Frame.program owns the resulting activation. The existing general dispatch loop changes its borrowed execution view only when frame ownership changes. Entry program/realm are restored on return or error. Native/host tails discard guest context, locals/register references, environment and dynamic roots before the rooted host invocation; the host call returns directly from the frame. Tail backedges collect only after the replacement frame publishes callee roots. Ordinary Wasm calls remain non-tail, including calls followed by Return. No opcode, extra executor, wrapper or format change.",
  "sources": [
